    'Cfhr3 is the mouse ortholog of human CFHR3. Think host defense, tolerance, and inflammatory signaling. Native regulation knockins beat random overexpression for dosage sensitive cytokines like Cfhr3. Reporter alleles let you track Cfhr3 positive cells during challenge without permanently removing the pathway. Humanize for antibody work on CFHR3. Use mouse nulls when you only need pathway necessity. Pair a humanized Cfhr3 target with a human immune engraftment host if the readout is a biologic. Single locus mutants often understate combination biology. Checkpoint or cytokine partner crosses are common with Cfhr3.',
  Cfi:
    'Human CFI maps to mouse Cfi. That is the locus for host defense, tolerance, and inflammatory signaling. If systemic loss confounds the read, restrict the deletion. Do not force a global null for a cell type question. Inducible Cre after immune education finishes separates developmental effects from adult effector function. Human sequence at Cfi also helps when your diagnostic reagent only recognizes the human protein. Reporter alleles let you track Cfi positive cells during challenge without permanently removing the pathway.',
  Cflar:
    'For immune work on host defense, tolerance, and inflammatory signaling, Cflar is the allele most people build. If the assay is antibody blockade of CFLAR, humanize Cflar early. Use mouse nulls to show pathway need. If systemic loss confounds the read, restrict the deletion. Do not force a global null for a cell type question. Inducible Cre after immune education finishes separates developmental effects from adult effector function. Pick the Cre that matches the compartment in your primary assay before you lock the allele.',
  Chchd10:
    'Circuit and disease studies of Chchd10 are really about circuit function or neurodegeneration. Region restricted deletion avoids developmental wiring defects that hide adult neurodegeneration phenotypes at Chchd10. Wiring, acute injury, and chronic proteinopathy need different KO versus knockin choices. If the binder only recognizes human CHCHD10, humanize Chchd10 before you invest in a large behavior study. Most neuroscience programs need some mix of null, floxed, knockin, and humanized Chchd10 alleles. Antibody and ASO programs need human sequence at Chchd10. Mouse only genetics leave a gap.',
  Chchd2:
    'If the question is circuit function or neurodegeneration, Chchd2 is the locus I would build. Pairing Chchd2 with a known neurodegeneration allele can reveal synergy that single locus genetics miss. Region restricted deletion avoids developmental wiring defects that hide adult neurodegeneration phenotypes at Chchd2. Wiring, acute injury, and chronic proteinopathy need different KO versus knockin choices. Reporter alleles map Chchd2 across neuron and glia subtypes without removing function. For motor, memory, or survival curves, adult inducible loss or human variant knockins beat constitutive KO.',
  Chd4:
    'Tumor studies of Chd4 start from driver signaling, DNA repair, or tumor niche biology. Humanize Chd4 when the antibody, ADC, or degrader needs human CHD4 sequence in a mouse host. Inducible timing lets you treat established disease instead of nascent lesions. If the null is embryonic lethal, go conditional or mosaic. Do not force a homozygous knockout for an adult tumor study. Most oncology programs escalate across null, floxed, knockin, and humanized Chd4 alleles. Patient variant knockins get you into pharmacology that matches clinical CHD4 mutations.',
  Chek1:
    'Chek1 is the mouse ortholog of human CHEK1. The question people bring is usually DNA repair and checkpoint control. Point mutant knockins make sense when human CHEK1 variants change activity instead of removing the protein. Most programs need some mix of null, floxed, knockin, and humanized Chek1 alleles as the question evolves. A human exon knockin at Chek1 avoids false negatives from sequence drift in antibody studies. Floxed Chek1 plus a Cre you trust is enough for most adult signaling readouts.',
  Chek2:
    'Chek2 is the mouse form of CHEK2. Most adult work here is really about DNA repair and checkpoint control. If viability is unclear, flox first. Do not sink a colony into a constitutive null until you know. Point mutant knockins make sense when human CHEK2 variants change activity instead of removing the protein. If the compound only binds human CHEK2, humanize first and use a mouse null for mechanism. If a related family member can compensate, plan the second conditional cross up front or the phenotype will look cleaner than it is.',
  Chrd:
    'Developmental work on Chrd is about buffering BMP and related morphogens. Expect early lethality risk. Timed inducible alleles separate embryonic patterning failure from adult repair involving Chrd. Humanize Chrd for biologics and ligand traps that bind human CHRD more tightly than mouse protein. Match Cre geography to the field that actually expresses Chrd. Hypomorphic knockins can mimic human CHRD dosage syndromes better than complete nulls when partial function is the clinical picture. Most morphogen programs need some mix of null, floxed, knockin, and humanized Chrd alleles.',
  Cntnap2:
    'If the question is circuit function or neurodegeneration, Cntnap2 is the locus I would build. Pairing Cntnap2 with a known neurodegeneration allele can reveal synergy that single locus genetics miss. For adult brain questions, cKO or disease knockins beat harsh developmental nulls. Disease knockins beat overexpression transgenes when dosage and splicing matter for human CNTNAP2 proteotoxicity. Wiring, acute injury, and chronic proteinopathy need different KO versus knockin choices. If the binder only recognizes human CNTNAP2, humanize Cntnap2 before you invest in a large behavior study.',
  Coq2:
    'Coq2 is the mouse ortholog of human COQ2. Neuro work here is about circuit function or neurodegeneration. Disease knockins beat overexpression transgenes when dosage and splicing matter for human COQ2 proteotoxicity. If the binder only recognizes human COQ2, humanize Coq2 before you invest in a large behavior study. Humanize when the drug needs human COQ2 sequence. Antibody and ASO programs need human sequence at Coq2. Mouse only genetics leave a gap. If you need aged cohorts, decide early whether you want a strong null or a milder hypomorphic knockin at Coq2.',
  Coq3:
    'For circuit function or neurodegeneration, you want precise Coq3 genetics without losing animals before aging windows open. Antibody and ASO programs need human sequence at Coq3. Mouse only genetics leave a gap. If you need aged cohorts, decide early whether you want a strong null or a milder hypomorphic knockin at Coq3. For adult brain questions, cKO or disease knockins beat harsh developmental nulls. Humanize Coq3 when pathology depends on human specific isoforms or aggregation sequences in COQ3. Disease knockins beat overexpression transgenes when dosage and splicing matter for human COQ3 proteotoxicity.',
