  Coq9:
    'Coq9 (COQ9) comes up when you need clean genetics for circuit function or neurodegeneration. If the binder only recognizes human COQ9, humanize Coq9 before you invest in a large behavior study. Inducible neuronal or glial Cre separates cell autonomous stress from support cell contributions. In brain work, Cre choice is part of the design. Do not treat it as an afterthought. Pairing Coq9 with a known neurodegeneration allele can reveal synergy that single locus genetics miss. Region restricted deletion avoids developmental wiring defects that hide adult neurodegeneration phenotypes at Coq9.',
  Cox10:
    'If you are running diet or physiology studies on energy balance and organ level metabolism, Cox10 is the allele. Knockins that mimic human COX10 coding variants go beyond simple loss of function. Humanize Cox10 when antibodies, enzyme replacements, or peptides are built on human COX10 rather than mouse protein. Glucose, lipid, and cardiovascular readouts often need different Cre geography. Inducible adult deletion cuts developmental metabolic confounds that show up in constitutive Cox10 nulls. Most cardio metabolic programs need some mix of null, floxed, knockin, and humanized Cox10 alleles.',
  Cox11:
    'Cox11 (COX11) is what I would build for energy balance and organ level metabolism. For sequence selective biologics, humanize Cox11 for efficacy and keep mouse nulls for mechanism. Whole body knockout still helps for circulating factors when tissue source matters less than systemic loss of Cox11. Tissue specific deletion plus a controlled diet beats an untimed global null for most drug studies. Reporter knockins show tissue induction during fasting or obesity without changing coding sequence. Liver, adipose, muscle, or kidney restricted alleles tell you which organ supplies the Cox11 phenotype under diet challenge.',
  Cox14:
    'For energy balance and organ level metabolism, build Cox14 as the mouse form of COX14. Whole body knockout still helps for circulating factors when tissue source matters less than systemic loss of Cox14. Reporter knockins show tissue induction during fasting or obesity without changing coding sequence. Organ restricted cKO maps the source. Humanize when the therapeutic is built on human COX14. Liver, adipose, muscle, or kidney restricted alleles tell you which organ supplies the Cox14 phenotype under diet challenge. Glucose, lipid, and cardiovascular readouts often need different Cre geography.',
  Cox15:
    'Cox15 is the mouse ortholog of human COX15. The biology is energy balance and organ level metabolism. Transgenic overexpression models pathway gain when the hypothesis is agonism rather than loss of Cox15. If related metabolic nodes may compensate, plan challenge diets and partner genetics with the primary Cox15 allele. Inducible adult alleles avoid developmental compensation in energy balance circuits involving Cox15. Pharmacodynamic studies often need a humanized target plus a diet inducible disease background. Knockins that mimic human COX15 coding variants go beyond simple loss of function.',
