  Mmp1:
    'For immune work on matrix remodeling and cell adhesion, Mmp1 is the allele most people build. Single locus mutants often understate combination biology. Checkpoint or cytokine partner crosses are common with Mmp1. Humanize Mmp1 when clinical antibodies see human MMP1 epitopes that mouse protein lacks. Pick the Cre that matches the compartment in your primary assay before you lock the allele. Inducible Cre after immune education finishes separates developmental effects from adult effector function. KO, cKO, knockin, and humanized Mmp1 alleles are what most immune programs actually need.',
  Mmp12:
    'Mmp12 (MMP12) comes up constantly in infection, autoimmunity, and tumor challenge. Reporter alleles let you track Mmp12 positive cells during challenge without permanently removing the pathway. Pair a humanized Mmp12 target with a human immune engraftment host if the readout is a biologic. For immuno oncology, humanized targets in the right immune context beat mouse only nulls. Single locus mutants often understate combination biology. Checkpoint or cytokine partner crosses are common with Mmp12. If systemic loss confounds the read, restrict the deletion. Do not force a global null for a cell type question.',
