  Pcsk9:
    'For glucose, lipid, and energy sensing, start with Pcsk9 rather than a random overexpression construct. I flox Pcsk9 first. Keep a null only if you need a severity benchmark or a rescue cross. A Pcsk9 allele crossed to a pathway partner often beats studying the gene alone. If viability is unclear, flox first. Do not sink a colony into a constitutive null until you know. Humanize Pcsk9 when your antibody or degrader prefers human PCSK9 over mouse protein. Point mutant knockins make sense when human PCSK9 variants change activity instead of removing the protein.',
  Pdcd1:
    'Pdcd1 encodes PD1, a major immune checkpoint. Mouse models of Pdcd1 clarified how blockade reinvigorates T cells and set expectations that human trials later confirmed. Conditional alleles help dissect tissue resident versus circulating pools of PD1 signaling. Humanized lines align murine epitopes with therapeutic antibodies. These animals remain core infrastructure for combination oncology and for mechanistic studies of exhaustion.',
  Pdcd1lg2:
    'If you need genetics for host defense, tolerance, and inflammatory signaling, start with Pdcd1lg2. Some papers also call it PD L2. Delete Pdcd1lg2 in T cells, B cells, myeloid cells, or epithelium if you need to know which compartment drives the phenotype. If the assay is antibody blockade of PDCD1LG2, humanize Pdcd1lg2 early. Use mouse nulls to show pathway need. If systemic loss confounds the read, restrict the deletion. Do not force a global null for a cell type question.',
  Pdgfra:
    'Tumor studies of Pdgfra start from driver signaling, DNA repair, or tumor niche biology. Tissue restricted or inducible alleles let tumors arise after development, closer to how patients acquire PDGFRA lesions. Add humanized checkpoint partners when the readout is immunotherapy rather than tumor genetics alone. Most oncology programs escalate across null, floxed, knockin, and humanized Pdgfra alleles. If the biologic fails to cross react with mouse Pdgfra, humanization is required, not optional. A conventional knockout works for tumor suppressor dosage if homozygous Pdgfra loss is tolerated long enough to score tumors.',
  Pdgfrb:
    'Pdgfrb (PDGFRB) shows up on therapy and resistance paths that need defined cohorts. Most oncology programs escalate across null, floxed, knockin, and humanized Pdgfrb alleles. A conventional knockout works for tumor suppressor dosage if homozygous Pdgfrb loss is tolerated long enough to score tumors. Orthotopic designs with engineered Pdgfrb alleles beat simple overexpression grafts for niche questions. Crossing Pdgfrb to Kras, Trp53, or Myc is still the standard way to test cooperation and therapy response. Suppressors: flox or null. Drivers: activating knockin. Biologics aimed at PDGFRB: humanize.',
