  Rptor:
    'For Pi3K Akt mTOR growth control, start with Rptor rather than a random overexpression construct. A human exon knockin at Rptor avoids false negatives from sequence drift in antibody studies. Adult deletion of Rptor is usually cleaner than taking it out from birth. If viability is unclear, flox first. Do not sink a colony into a constitutive null until you know. Humanize Rptor when your antibody or degrader prefers human RPTOR over mouse protein. Point mutant knockins make sense when human RPTOR variants change activity instead of removing the protein.',
  Runx1:
    'Runx1 is the mouse ortholog of human RUNX1. Oncology work here is about driver signaling, DNA repair, or tumor niche biology. For oncogenes, activating knockins beat simple deletion of Runx1. Most oncology programs escalate across null, floxed, knockin, and humanized Runx1 alleles. Patient variant knockins get you into pharmacology that matches clinical RUNX1 mutations. If early lethality kills the adult tumor window, start with conditional Runx1. Orthotopic designs with engineered Runx1 alleles beat simple overexpression grafts for niche questions. Tissue restricted or inducible alleles let tumors arise after development, closer to how patients acquire RUNX1 lesions.',
