    'For driver signaling, DNA repair, or tumor niche biology in a mouse, build Runx1t1 as the ortholog of RUNX1T1. Some papers also call it ETO. Patient variant knockins get you into pharmacology that matches clinical RUNX1T1 mutations. Crossing Runx1t1 to Kras, Trp53, or Myc is still the standard way to test cooperation and therapy response. Suppressors: flox or null. Drivers: activating knockin. Biologics aimed at RUNX1T1: humanize. Humanize Runx1t1 when the antibody, ADC, or degrader needs human RUNX1T1 sequence in a mouse host.',
  Rxra:
    'Developmental work on Rxra is about making, clearing, or sensing retinoic acid. Expect early lethality risk. Timed inducible alleles separate embryonic patterning failure from adult repair involving Rxra. Humanize Rxra for biologics and ligand traps that bind human RXRA more tightly than mouse protein. Match Cre geography to the field that actually expresses Rxra. Hypomorphic knockins can mimic human RXRA dosage syndromes better than complete nulls when partial function is the clinical picture. Most morphogen programs need some mix of null, floxed, knockin, and humanized Rxra alleles.',
